{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5","id":608558,"title":"disciplines level above 5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-30T16:14:59-07:00","id":608558,"title":"disciplines level above 5","content":"Do exist any official example of disciplines powers above fifth for the second edition of requiem? Or any unofficial but plausible homemade powers on web??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:18:30-07:00","id":608585,"title":"","content":"Look for the Disciplines in Vampire: the Masquerade, for any previous example. But remember it isn't the same system and you have to be aware of the differences.<br /> <br /> By the rule I think there are no Discipline level above 5 in Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:30:05-07:00","id":608598,"title":"","content":"Requiem has no Disciplines over five dots. Potent, elder level powers are the domain of Devotions. There are numerous Devotions in Requiem 2e that really only work for high Potency vampires (Juggernauts Gait comes to mind). You might also check <b>Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners</b>, the character Zagreus has a particularly potent Devotion requiring Blood Potency 6+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:37:19-07:00","id":608604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=608585#post608585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look for the Disciplines in Vampire: the Masquerade, for any previous example. But remember it isn't the same system and you have to be aware of the differences.<br /> <br /> By the rule I think there are no Discipline level above 5 in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, not always ideal - many of VtM's elder powers were actually pretty underwhelming stuff that was bumped into level 6+ due to how rigid the disciplines were back then without devotions and other options.<br /> <br /> Possibly of interest, the only NPC with an official sample of a Dominate 6 power that i know of: <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/VtR_Melissidae_MadonnaOfTheWasps.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pd...OfTheWasps.pdf</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T21:50:24-07:00","id":608921,"title":"","content":"Far from ideal, indeed. I just said it was the only source of examples. Tough the game hints to this possibility, it never really used it except by this Melissa.<br /> <br /> I agree that Devotions are the best way to handle such power level.<br /> <br /> But if you do want to work it, Masquerade will at least have examples. They're wildly unbalanced, though. And the 9th and 10th levels where never meant for PCs, even 8th level barely was, 6th and 7th just for high-level chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  correcting a 6 years old typo. 08-14-2021, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T02:53:46-07:00","id":609200,"title":"","content":"Rules As Written I believe you can't have a discipline at higher than 5, although I will agree that it can be misinterpreted by clever reading. Only Attributes and Skills can go above 5 due to the wording on the table, which makes the question of 'can a vampire with high enough Blood Potency (or generation, the problem exists in Masquerade) have Resources 6? If so why not someone with only three dots?'<br /> <br /> Of course, the RAW only matters as far as you let it, if you want 6+ Disciplines go ahead. I personally plan on ignoring the feeding restrictions chart for at least a Chronicle and instead have elder vampires enter torpor from a lack of touchstones (which would be required to be living people). If, in your game, powerful enough vampires can dominate over the internet that's fine, as long as you don't complain that it isn't official.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T03:30:21-07:00","id":609237,"title":"","content":"I personally think of 6+ powers to be methuselah transformation stuff, like in Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T05:49:48-07:00","id":609291,"title":"","content":"In first edition 6+ level Disciplines where said to exist, but never worked upon, what's ok in my book. In 2nd they aren't even cited, indeed.<br /> <br /> Since I didn't read Imperial Mysteries yet I can't say for sure, but I also reached the same conclusion. If Mages can reach Archmastery, there are no reason for other splats not to do so in a way. But I'm personaly inclined to veto Archmastery in my chronicles and not even consider them existing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T06:34:11-07:00","id":609315,"title":"","content":"Archmastery makes sense for mages in a way that arch-vampirism can't really match. An archmaster is someone who pushed up to a very literal boundary to power and forced their way through. It's more than just an extra dot. It's a fundamental change in the very nature of their being. There's no such boundary for vampires. At five dots you know all there is to know about the discipline and can make new powers based on the same principles all you like. There are no 6 dot powers in requiem because there doesn't <i>need </i> to be. A vampire can already do everything imaginable at 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:12:45-07:00","id":609362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609315#post609315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archmastery makes sense for mages in a way that arch-vampirism can't really match. An archmaster is someone who pushed up to a very literal boundary to power and forced their way through. It's more than just an extra dot. It's a fundamental change in the very nature of their being. There's no such boundary for vampires. At five dots you know all there is to know about the discipline and can make new powers based on the same principles all you like. There are no 6 dot powers in requiem because there doesn't <i>need </i> to be. A vampire can already do everything imaginable at 5.</div> </div> </div> </div> Methuselah are fundamentally changed from regular elders, just as archmasters are fundamentally changed from mere Masters. A sixth dot discipline is just one way to represent that evolution. <br /> <br /> In short - &quot;6th dot powers are how I represent an evolution to a tier 4 cosmic-level game.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:41:44-07:00","id":609608,"title":"","content":"What MCN said.<br /> <br /> In other words: First, if you think so, you never saw the concept of methuselah vampire or similar in an RPG before. By the way, they existed in Masquerade, even if you can argue the quality of the rules. But the concept is there, and isn't that far in scope from archmastery.<br /> <br /> Second, plain balance. If one splat has the right to this level of power, all splats have. That's a rule of mine for nWoD games. When I don't want this kind of basic balance I go for cWoD, where the equivalent of a BP 10 vampire was able to survive days and nights of sunlight + epic battle + state-of-the-art archmage constructed atomic bomb, and only died when already weakened he was shot by Sattelite Sun Ray Of Hellish Doom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:49:20-07:00","id":609616,"title":"","content":"OK, but devotions can get pretty bonkers. Imagine, just for a second, what you could potentially do with a power that had every discipline in the book at 5 dots as a prerequisite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:39:30-07:00","id":609742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609616#post609616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but devotions can get pretty bonkers. Imagine, just for a second, what you could potentially do with a power that had every discipline in the book at 5 dots as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Super-death-beauty-illusion-speed-strike-command?<br /> <br /> I don't think you can really combine all 10, but Dominate 5+Majesty 5+Nightmare 5 and Animalism 5+Protean 5+Majesty 5 are two devotions that practical no vampires will develop. You don't even need to go beyond two Disciplines at 5 to start getting as powerful as Masquerade's good elder-level powers.<br /> <br /> You will never be able to beat Zepher though, as soon as I find out what moving that fast actually does rules-wise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:47:44-07:00","id":609743,"title":"","content":"Yes ok but for example celerity at 5 means a vampire can run at about 300 km/h...a lot but not so &quot;epic&quot;. A vampire with BP 7-8 could reach really awsome speed like in the Anna Rice's books or similar. Same for Vigor....and resilence too. Why a BP 7-8 vampire must have the same ability to ignore damage from fire or other source like a BP 5 vampire?? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:50:38-07:00","id":609744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, plain balance. If one splat has the right to this level of power, all splats have. </div> </div> </div>What about it not making narrative sense? Archmasters aren't just magi but bigger metaphorically, they encompass rewriting reality. They're not a normal part of a mage chronicle, but they're an implication of the setting and they work well with that setting. Trying to balance that with Requiem a different game with different tone and scope is pointless and is just going to damage Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:05:43-07:00","id":609754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609743#post609743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y Why a BP 7-8 vampire must have the same ability to ignore damage from fire or other source like a BP 5 vampire??</div> </div> </div> </div>Because BP5 is where &quot;outright invulnerable&quot; becomes a viable option and it's tough to go up from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:54:12-07:00","id":609901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609744#post609744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about it not making narrative sense? Archmasters aren't just magi but bigger metaphorically, they encompass rewriting reality. They're not a normal part of a mage chronicle, but they're an implication of the setting and they work well with that setting. Trying to balance that with Requiem a different game with different tone and scope is pointless and is just going to damage Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>And from where you get the idea that a similar expansion on the themes and implications of the setting isn't possible for other splats?<br /> <br /> Long before White Wolf, a lot of vampire stories where about truly ancient and powerful beings. In Dracula the &quot;evil count&quot; is far more powerful than his wives and servitors. Castlevania depicts a Lord of Darkness able to comand the creatures of the night enough to theaten the whole world. The Queen of the Damned is the most powerful being on Anne Rice's novels. Through and through, the ancient vampire rising from torpor to bring darkness upon the living is much more a staple of the genre than archmasters.<br /> <br /> In the end it is just a little effort and you can bring not only a reasonable explanation to every splat achieving that degree of power, but one that truly makes the setting more interesting.<br /> <br /> Or you can just get rid of the Archmasters, because no, it isn't a natural implication of the setting. Just one possibility like infinite others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:00:10-07:00","id":609917,"title":"","content":"The thing is you don't need more than five dots to demonstrate further degrees of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:18:04-07:00","id":609944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609616#post609616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but devotions can get pretty bonkers. Imagine, just for a second, what you could potentially do with a power that had every discipline in the book at 5 dots as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>As others have said, there's something of a limit to how many disciplines can be comboed in a devotion (3 at most, think), but yeah, devotions open the room for a lot of crazy custom stuff and character individuality on a vampire's powers (even inserted learning your 1st devotion and creating one's own to breaking points because of this. Elder devotions expand the range/scale of one's options even further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609743#post609743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes ok but for example celerity at 5 means a vampire can run at about 300 km/h...a lot but not so &quot;epic&quot;. A vampire with BP 7-8 could reach really awsome speed like in the Anna Rice's books or similar. Same for Vigor....and resilence too. Why a BP 7-8 vampire must have the same ability to ignore damage from fire or other source like a BP 5 vampire??</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, considering that at this level the only thing on the planet faster than you are <b>airplanes</b>, i would say &quot;not epic&quot; can be pretty relative, specially if a vampire has the Forced March devotion. Not to mention Celerity might be said enhances one's <b>reponse time</b> in the same proportion as one's speed, a benefit no racer ever can brag about and one of the motives the virtual speed limit for cars and other stuff is around that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609901#post609901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And from where you get the idea that a similar expansion on the themes and implications of the setting isn't possible for other splats?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think his point is more &quot;yeah, it can be done, but is it worth it?&quot; Themes go beyond power and scale - elder devotions are already one way of adressing it, in fact. Sometimes a adapting the themes of another game can have quite unexpected or undesirable results, even when done right. The divisiviness and &quot;sour taste&quot; Blood Sorcery's magic system seem to have left, with fans and authors after it came out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-31-2015, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:19:10-07:00","id":609959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609917#post609917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is you don't need more than five dots to demonstrate further degrees of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case an exception should are the physical disciplines like celerity...imho","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:34:21-07:00","id":609965,"title":"","content":"The problem with physical disciplines over Five Dots is, IMO, not that they are game breaking or unfair, quite the opposite; they are really underwhelming.<br /> <br /> Think about it, how many instances is your vampire going to need to negate <b>more</b> than 6 levels of damage per attack? Or punch with greater than a +5 weapon bonus? Are there that many fights where interrupting five times isn't enough? Just compare theoretical elders here: Ones got Celerity, Vigor and Resilience at 10! A real beast, supposedly. But consider now the same character could instead have Celerity, Resilience and Vigor 5, Dominate 5, Auspex 4, Obfuscate 3, and a couple devotions (like Juggernaut's Gait).<br /> <br /> Now I don't know about you, but that second character seems like the more interesting, and more effective choice. Unless we're working is stupid white-room battle ground (which has no bearing on actual play), elder #2 is just as good as elder #1 in 99% of scenarios, plus he's equipped with a boatload of additional options (Mind control, Invisibility, Insight) that allow him to excel in far more interesting ways.<br /> <br /> Basically: The notion that more dots = more power is, practically speaking, false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:55:05-07:00","id":610005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609744#post609744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about it not making narrative sense? Archmasters aren't just magi but bigger metaphorically, they encompass rewriting reality. They're not a normal part of a mage chronicle, but they're an implication of the setting and they work well with that setting. Trying to balance that with Requiem a different game with different tone and scope is pointless and is just going to damage Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampire has the Methusalha (or however you spell it) as their big, beyond-elder thing. Werewolf has wolf totems. Changeling has becoming one of the Gentry. In Geist, we've had Sin-Eater NPCs turn Keroberus, and theoretically from there, into death gods. The Deceived in Mummy can become aspects of Fate. We don't know what happens when a Demon gains Hell, and I imagine that a Beast that's reached their Inheritance is giong to be nothing to sneer at either. <br /> <br /> Lots of games already have archmage equivalents that make cosmological and narrative sense, and are part of the story. We don't necessarily have the rules for all of them, but then, at that power level, we don't really need it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=609965#post609965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically: The notion that more dots = more power is, practically speaking, false.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, its still more power. Its just that we reached the point where its overkill, if we assume 6+ dots are linear growth. <br /> <br /> I'm personally not too concerned about dots over 6, especially not for Supernatural Tolerances. Yes, in theory, you can get very powerful. But I find that the game math starts to break down, and the game gets silly from there. Its the type of end-game thing I don't usually play in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:00:23-07:00","id":610008,"title":"","content":"I wounder, why this specific topic came back again and again. I thought everything about it has been said.<br /> <br /> For example in this threads to just take the most recent ones:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped\"> Are Physical Disciplines Uncapped? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There is nothing in Blood and Smoke that says Disciplines have any form of limit (unless I'm missing something). Does that mean that you can keep purchasing Disciplines (particularly things like Celerity, Vigor, and Resilience) infinitely? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks\"> Are there 6+ dots disciplines ranks? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> OK, now I sound like a total newbie. So, in yet another if-it-exists-in-VtM-does-it-in-VtR, are there 6+ dots Disciplines, stuff that you could only unlock with very high blood potency, or that elder vampires would be known to have and would drive fear in the heart of players? If so, in what book, because I </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:04:53-07:00","id":610011,"title":"","content":"It would be cool to have a sort of FAQ that could link to these things, they do come up often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:06:46-07:00","id":610013,"title":"","content":"I'm not saing that have celerity vigor and resilence at 10 means be more powerful then a vampire with just majesty that could make him is consensient slave. I just saing that is weird that attribute skills and other things can rise over 5 but not the discipline. Ok don't consider physical discipline cause are not well seen here XD. But with devotion you can mix different effects from different disciplines but not make a discipline more powerful. For example, domination: you can mix with other discipline but rising his power level you could obtain more powerful and unique effect (like the ezample of domination 6 proposed in an upper post that allow to dominate an huge group of people).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:10:09-07:00","id":610017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=610013#post610013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, domination: you can mix with other discipline but rising his power level you could obtain more powerful and unique effect (like the ezample of domination 6 proposed in an upper post that allow to dominate an huge group of people).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Majesty does. You'd do that by making a devotion with Dominate and Majesty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:51:06-07:00","id":610244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=610008#post610008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wounder, why this specific topic came back again and again. I thought everything about it has been said.<br /> <br /> For example in this threads to just take the most recent ones:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped\"> Are Physical Disciplines Uncapped? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/402794-are-physical-disciplines-uncapped </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> There is nothing in Blood and Smoke that says Disciplines have any form of limit (unless I'm missing something). Does that mean that you can keep purchasing Disciplines (particularly things like Celerity, Vigor, and Resilience) infinitely? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/487155-are-there-6-dots-disciplines-ranks\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ciplines-ranks</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Freshness of the subject to a person may vary according to previous familiarity with the forum. Some people are more used to/confortable with the VtM frame, others look at MtAw's many possibilities of growth, expansion and sense of scale and wish for some of that out of a sense of simmetry or a desire to &quot;buff&quot; their pet supernatural in a similar way, not to mention those who want further detail of an early concept (elder powers) that seems to have been mostly abandoned or developed in a non-linear manner.<br /> <br /> And sometimes you just don't get the right words in your search tool, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T19:10:38-07:00","id":610252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=610244#post610244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not to mention those who want further detail of an early concept (elder powers) that seems to have been mostly abandoned or developed in a non-linear manner.</div> </div> </div> </div>To those I would suggest looking at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">publishing schedule</a> under A Thousand Years of Night, or maybe searching the forums for it, as it is a book about elders and what makes them different from younger vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:10:33-07:00","id":610305,"title":"","content":"To be fair about the argument that you don't need more dots than five... I agree with that. I can change my mind when I do read Imperial Masteries, because that's kind of my point, see what they did there, but still.<br /> <br /> An approach I'm actualy surprised no one brought was the One Discipline Devotion. The core book already shows one of that, for Obfuscate. Juggernaut's Gait also shows how you can stretch the concept of a single power, even if it have more than one as pre-req. I don't think you should measure the power of a Devotion based upon its pre-reqs alone, but you can use Devotions to improve Disciplines in the ways that more interest you. Far better than just making them above 5th level. As an example, you could make a Devotion with pre-reqs Celerity 5 + BP 6+ that improves your speed during Celerity to be calculated based upon BP instead of just Celerity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think his point is more &quot;yeah, it can be done, but is it worth it?&quot; Themes go beyond power and scale - elder devotions are already one way of adressing it, in fact. Sometimes a adapting the themes of another game can have quite unexpected or undesirable results, even when done right. The divisiviness and &quot;sour taste&quot; Blood Sorcery's magic system seem to have left, with fans and authors after it came out...</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it is already a trope, as I pointed before, I think it is worth it, or at least as worth as Archmastery. The perceived balance between splats also have impact on the WoD setting, it is also an important theme as you can always be sure both that your equals can achieve god-like power as that even them there are things out there that can munch you. And I'm not talking about adapt the theme of another game, but use the themes and tropes of each gameline to work the same scale, if you want to work such scale.<br /> <br /> Either way, I have yet to read Imperial Mysteries to say how and <b>if</b> it should be translated into rules. For now, Devotions do work pretty well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I don't know about you, but that second character seems like the more interesting, and more effective choice. Unless we're working is stupid white-room battle ground (which has no bearing on actual play), elder #2 is just as good as elder #1 in 99% of scenarios, plus he's equipped with a boatload of additional options (Mind control, Invisibility, Insight) that allow him to excel in far more interesting ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>White-room battles aren't stupid, unless you think the system shouldn't have any to do with mathematics, and them I would say the notion of a system itself becomes moot. That said, tough, the second case will be more effective even in the white-room. The first will overkill with those disciplines, but not that much. Most of them will be less effective precisely for being so high it becomes meaningless, whyle the other can use Obfuscate to sneak behind the no-Auspex hulk and deny it Defense (Celerity included), or Dominate him into submission, or keep the fight at a distance and win because he have the Devotion needed to use Defense against Firearms and his normal Defense is already 8 before Celerity (and can be greater)...<br /> <br /> You have in the second a character with far more resources, both to accomplish different things and to effectively acomplish the same ones. You are pretty right, I just think the &quot;white-rooms are stupid&quot; argument lame and unnecessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wounder, why this specific topic came back again and again. I thought everything about it has been said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't matter how many times a question is answered, there will always be someone who never heard the answer. The question is bound to exist, and to repeat itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But with devotion you can mix different effects from different disciplines but not make a discipline more powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cloak the Gathering (Obfuscate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), in B&amp;S page 142.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T21:15:17-07:00","id":610366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=610305#post610305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have in the second a character with far more resources, both to accomplish different things and to effectively acomplish the same ones. You are pretty right, I just think the &quot;white-rooms are stupid&quot; argument lame and unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Rooms are pretty ill respected on these forums. Indeed I'm one of the few people who will argue their value. So I'll amend that statement to: All conclusions drawn from such a white room (which, IMO, is too vague to draw any) are unlikely to reflect practical play.<br /> <br /> White Rooms aren't stupid. But people often draw wildly inaccurate conclusions from them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T21:31:37-07:00","id":610373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=610366#post610366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Rooms aren't stupid. But people often draw wildly inaccurate conclusions from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T21:50:08-07:00","id":610383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=610305#post610305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it is already a trope, as I pointed before, I think it is worth it, or at least as worth as Archmastery. The perceived balance between splats also have impact on the WoD setting, it is also an important theme as you can always be sure both that your equals can achieve god-like power as that even them there are things out there that can munch you. And I'm not talking about adapt the theme of another game, but use the themes and tropes of each gameline to work the same scale, if you want to work such scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, why?<br /> <br /> There's no reason for every line to follow the same standard. They're, from the ground up, already not balanced against each other, and it makes even less sense for all of them to have a &quot;next level&quot; state that is roughly equal in power to all the others if their cosmologies don't lend themselves to it and work on very different paradigms and weight in respect to the World Of Darkness as a whole.<br /> <br /> Pretending that this is necessary to ensure the lines are 'balanced' in their setting space by being able to operate at the same scale uniformly is also a shaky notion at best, considering the rarity of these ascended states and the narrative role of the characters that occupy this level of power, which often ensures they are detached from the struggles that entangle the vast majority of the splat and don't tend to visibly operate or interfere with that layer of the story and don't usually influence it in a way that is felt by most, if they do at all; much less when dealing with the other game lines! The spheres would only cross in the advent of truly world-shaking events occurring in the scope of a common domain or large scale concept that matters to different supernatural beings, before causing more widespread conflict down the pyramid of power; assuming the matter would not be taken over, interrupted, or another manner of stopping event entirely within the range of action of these superior beings, without even affecting those that are not at the same level.<br /> <br /> And finally, the World Of Darkness is only as comprehensive and inclusive as you wish for it to be, so there's no need to worry about enforcing some artificial line of balance between Templates+ when their presence might not even be considered relevant at all or true depending on the chronicle. And of course that goes for the regular Templates as well.<br /> <br /> P.S.: I mean, I guess if that sort of major, reality defining conflict between every splat is someone's thing, sure go ahead, but it doesn't really lend itself to most of them IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-01-2015, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T02:46:00-07:00","id":610592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=610383#post610383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, why?<br /> There's no reason for every line to follow the same standard.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pax Arcana implies that there is a reason, at least from the Mage side. &quot;We archmasters usually don't mess with other supernaturals because their Patrons could cause us serious problems!&quot; Just sayin'. <br /> <br /> Its important for there to be roughly the same percieved balance because that is generally what people want when we think of such high level games. If Seers, the Diamond, and the FC were grossly more powerful than, say, elder vamps the world over, then the perception of the elders being a joke is spread, and that affects game play any time it comes up. Hunter defines itself by hunting other supernaturals, and power level does matter. <br /> <br /> The games aren't perfectly balanced against each other, but they are designed in a way where there is some. The ability to crossover is a selling point of the nWoD, even if the games don't thematically match up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:42:20-07:00","id":610634,"title":"","content":"Balance here isn't about true equilibrium, but about avoiding the perception that a given choice is &quot;better&quot; than other. It isn't an issue to some players, for sure. But is for others. And the game is for all (so to speak).<br /> <br /> Also, it can affect possibilities for chronicles, that is my main issue. When you bring new elements to the game, you creates more avenues for new stories to be told. Of course, some stories need the lack of some element, not its presence, but to withdraw is in some aspects easier than create.<br /> <br /> MCN actualy did a better job explaining, but I hope I had added to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:33:01-07:00","id":610809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=610252#post610252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To those I would suggest looking at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">publishing schedule</a> under A Thousand Years of Night, or maybe searching the forums for it, as it is a book about elders and what makes them different from younger vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, clearly i could have expressed myself iin the previous post, let me try again.<br /> <br /> I meant to say that elder powers <b>as a linear expansion of the discipline format</b> (aka powers 6-10) seems to have been mostly abandoned in preference for other, more branching venues to express peculiar might for elders. It was the apparent tendency in 1e material, though admitedly it remains to be seen how wrong or not will i be in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:04:03-07:00","id":610993,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain you will never see +6 Disciplines again.<br /> <br /> You'll definitely see high powered Devotions, though. The only +6 Discipline in any of the books was that Melissidae Supplement, and this was from the same fella who (it was a cool idea!) accidentally called Resilience Fortitude in other supplements, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:02:49-07:00","id":611511,"title":"","content":"@MCN, monteparnas:<br /> <br /> Imperial Mysteries pretty much opens up with &quot;the beings this book focuses on operate out of the scope of the other lines and make a stark difference in the rough balance of the setting, and we could avoid presenting them to maintain the integrity of crossover. But we're not, because this is what archmages are, and it would be a bit of a drag to not deliver on them as a logical followup to Mage.&quot;<br /> <br /> It goes on to say it assumes there are mechanisms to allow the other games to express themselves in a world where archmasters exist, so it's not going to tone the latter down to accomodate the former. What mechanisms those are is up to the storyteller, if it's even necessary to define them at all. So, like I said, if you feel like the other splats need equals to archmages to maintain their relevance, sure, go ahead. But that doesn't mean every game lends itself to it like mage does, as a natural stretch to their premise.<br /> <br /> See also my point about inclusivity in the World Of Darkness. I don't think the perception of balance is important, because not all monsters are equal, and not all monsters are the same. An elder vampire is scary. A master mage is scary. An apex werewolf is scary. But they're scary for different reasons and powerful in different ways. Vampire is strawberries, Mage is apples, and Werewolf is, uh, oranges*. And two werewolves may inspire awe for different things, and they'll be frightening to each other, to other werewolves and other supernaturals for those differing factors.<br /> <br /> Whatever perception of balance is necessary for the WoD, is at the most basic level taken care of by itself, in my opinion. It's not a matter of what's a &quot;better&quot; choice. They can't be compared like that, because they're all distinctive (and there aren't really any gross differences of power if we assume they share the shadows according to what each of their books establishes). And at the heights of Archmages, that equillibrium is even less necessary to present as an assumption of the setting, because beings that play on that level tend to matter very little indeed to what constitutes the core experience of the games of the World Of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: I don't think balance like that is necessary for crossover in the World Of Darkness, nor do I think the books are presented around that notion. But hey, it's the WoD. You can organize its features in your sandbox as you like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Because eating oranges is juicy and messy and.... okay I'm not sure where I was going with that. Like a werewolf family dinner? It's probably showing that it's late and I'm tired.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-01-2015, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:23:06-07:00","id":611663,"title":"","content":"If there's weighing in to do... I agree about the non-necessity for higher-end balance between lines. I envision some pretty scary-impressive ancient vampires, but that's nothing to what I envision when I think of an archmage. <br /> <br /> As long as there is flexibility in what is possible with Devotions on the high-end, I'm fine with the 5 dot limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T06:07:50-07:00","id":612131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=611511#post611511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bottom line: I don't think balance like that is necessary for crossover in the World Of Darkness, nor do I think the books are presented around that notion. But hey, it's the WoD. You can organize its features in your sandbox as you like.</div> </div> </div> </div> Bottom line: <u><i>Perception</i></u>of balance. Perception. You have constantly missed that very important detail. Its an important story concern when dealing with crossover. In crossover games, everyone needs to be able to function within their chosen niche without being overshadowed. Experience and feedback on crossover games has made this clear that its an active concern in such games. That's why <i>perception</i> is important. This expands to include NPCs and themes in the story as well.<br /> <br /> Can I ask how much experience you've had with crossover games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:44:13-07:00","id":612335,"title":"","content":"I have not missed that detail*. Like I said, I think the perception of balance takes care of itself where it matters. When it doesn't, it's because the take on the setting is being tilted to favor one line over another, and the portrayal of the world is failing to live up to the significance of each line**. If every game involved in the crossover is treated with the same weight their own book gives them, then there should in theory never be an issue with perception of balance. Any issues of the kind that may arise in a crossover game <i>come</i> <i>not </i><i>from an inherent flaw of the World Of Darkness</i><i>, but from the chronicle itself.</i><br /> <br /> (**The 'elder' monsters are all scary and identifiable as such, even to other supernaturals, and their overall numbers are also scary in comparison to each other. This is because they're different, and it's largely those differences that allow them to share the world of darkness without it coming down to the books making some of them seem straight &quot;better&quot; choices of Player Characters than others. Regardless of the fact that some of them may indeed be more powerful in straight confrontation as a general statement.)<br /> <br /> The World Of Darkness has never, in my opinion, had a problem with the presentation of one particular supernatural type making it seem vastly more powerful than the others.<br /> <br /> The Vampire chronicle my group was running had some subtle but important crossover, and our mortal campaign progressed into a supernatural crossover campaign, and never has any of us felt like one of the involved splats was getting shafted in favor of the others. So my personal experience with crossover isn't that much, but II regularly discuss it with one of my gaming buddies, so I think I have a pretty solid grasp of the topic all things considered.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*But it's a little annoying to have to type &quot;perception of balance&quot; every time. I don't believe it's hard to grasp that I have in fact been talking about the same topic as you.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-02-2015, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T11:32:12-07:00","id":612439,"title":"","content":"I have experience with crossovers since the 90's with cWoD. That setting took too long to understand the importance of said balance. Werewolf vs Vampire was all about UNbalance. Starting werewolfs where just too more powerful than starting vampires. Elder werewolfs where respectable heroes, whyle elder vampires where god-like. A 6th generation vampire with some centuries was powerful enough to wipe the floor with a Rank 4 pack. Both 6th generation and Rank 4 where concrete possibilities for players after some game time. Baba Yaga was a vampire so powerful she veiled the entire Russia against umbral expeditions for almost 10 years, enslaved packs of Silver Fangs of all ranks, and could only be destroyed by Deus Ex Machina, and you actualy got both the opportunity to sense her presence in the world, meet her and/or witness her demise in a published adventure. And a starting Demon can simply ignore the full extent of Dominate of an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> Those things affect the perception of balance in a variety of ways, even when they never enter play themselves. It impacts game experience. If you're into Mage, or like the notion that a mortal can somehow achieve such god-like power that no other creature lesser than &quot;true&quot; gods can compare, that's good, for sure. But if someone doesn't like the idea that a Mage can somehow attain such power, but others can't, this player will feel the spotlight going in the wrong direction. Even if at no moment at all this will actualy be more than a background collor.<br /> <br /> And again, its about options. With Imperial Mysteries there are the option for Archmasters to exist and play a role in my game. But I can simply rule them out of my chronicle. But I can't rule the Elder Vampires in, since there are no rules for them. That, and the fact, again, that there ARE possible tropes for the other splats going into this level of godhood.<br /> <br /> You don't see vampires achieving it in the same sense mages do? Well, to begin with, it doesn't have to be in the same sense. As the splats aren't about the same themes and tropes, but retain the perceived balance, you can expand all of them through <u>their</u> themes and <u>their</u> tropes, and achieve a perceived balance with Archmasters without being the same thing. The elder vampire IS a trope, and with longer tradition than the archmaster, mind you.<br /> <br /> Werewolfs can attain enough spiritual power to become god-like entities themselfs. Elder vampires can command the night itself, and control entire nations whyle their lesser kin struggle over a single city. Changelings can go to the kingdoms of the Fae, and return as gods of dream and madness themselves (actualy, thet had this option ALREADY on 1st ed, but as a loose-character scenario). Even Hunters can become true legends and go beyond the limits of mortals and monsters alike in their dedication (tough not yet worked in the nWoD, the special hunter that go beyond and necomes a nightmare to the monsters IS a common trope).<br /> <br /> But if you don't like them, you can allways simply rule them out. Each one just adds to the possibilities of the setting. You don't have to use them if you don't like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:06:38-07:00","id":612483,"title":"","content":"I think our disagreement on the subject comes down to the fact I don't feel a lack of perceived balance in the nWoD as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:18:39-07:00","id":612498,"title":"","content":"Plus, since an elder book with elder powers is on the schedule, and a similarity to 6+ powers can be emulated by tying requirements for devotions to Blood Potency, which runs to 10, the argument seems to be coming down to, 'Why didn't elders have a book last year?'<br /> <br /> Also I'd like to point out that archmastery is not something every mage gets into. Very few mages past 5 Gnosis end up becoming archmages. While every vampire who turns a certain age while remaining active is going to be an elder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-02-2015, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T12:48:07-07:00","id":612514,"title":"","content":"Archmages started out as plot devices. Even after they were made fully playable they remained plot devices for the normal mage level. The same is not true of elder vampires. Elders were never meant to be equal to Archmages in a narrative sense, so there is no reason for them to be balanced. Werewolves weren't supposed to have an analogue to Archmages at all. Luna and perhaps other uber spirits make sure archmages don't mess around with the werewolf species. Something does the same for vampires, and everything else.<br /> <br /> To a vampire, an archmage is a plot device. Vampires don't need to have power at that level. Given the paradigm of discipline power in 2E, anything a vampire should be able to do is going to be at the 5 dot level. A specific effect might require multiple disciplines at that level. High level vampires are equivalent to high level mages, not archmages. If we were trying to give vampires the equivalent to an archmage then having discipline go above 5 would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:08:52-07:00","id":612529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=612514#post612514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we were trying to give vampires the equivalent to an archmage then having discipline go above 5 would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Disciplines and arcarna are fundamentally different things. Arcarna are what makes a mage a mage. They are fundamentally defining things that represent a mages ability to mould reality to their will. By comparison disciplines are simple tricks, and from what we've seen there's nothing a sixth dot could do that a devotion couldn't. Their environmental niche is already filled, so they're either going to be ineffective at providing the balance you're seeking, or redundant. <br /> <br /> If you want to evolve a vampire past it's limits, you're going to need another mechanic for doing so entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:19:33-07:00","id":612639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5#post608558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do exist any official example of disciplines powers above fifth for the second edition of requiem? Or any unofficial but plausible homemade powers on web??</div> </div> </div> </div>There were some in first edition in some books but other approaches were done as well. And now 5 dot disciplines are much more powerful than what they were before.<br /> Some have even said the make 5 dot masquerade pale in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T17:29:34-07:00","id":612826,"title":"","content":"Honestly, now that single discipline devotions are a thing, there isn't really any reason to have 6+ disciplines. A dominate 1, BP 6 devotion could easily replicate the effects of first edition's dominate 6. Likewise, taking the physical disciplines all the way to 10 can be done with a series of single-discipline, bp 6+ devotions. <br /> <br /> All of the tools for Imperial Mystery-style powers are already there. As long as a devotion's constitute disciplines remain thematically appropriate for the effect you want to pull off, the only limit to a high bp vampire's capabilities is his imagination.<br /> <br /> That said, just because the tools are there doesn't mean I wouldn't mind a book that further details and presents guidelines for how to create such over-the-top devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7080-armadeo","name":"Armadeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T17:57:54-07:00","id":612864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=612529#post612529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Disciplines and arcarna are fundamentally different things. Arcarna are what makes a mage a mage. They are fundamentally defining things that represent a mages ability to mould reality to their will. By comparison disciplines are simple tricks, and from what we've seen there's nothing a sixth dot could do that a devotion couldn't. Their environmental niche is already filled, so they're either going to be ineffective at providing the balance you're seeking, or redundant.<br /> <br /> If you want to evolve a vampire past it's limits, you're going to need another mechanic for doing so entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>A new mechanic isn't <i>necessary</i>. You can do it with Disciplines, but you would need to accept that dots over 5 are fundamentally different than dots not over 5, which basically would be a new mechanic. You would need to make disciplines over 5 dots what they have said to be since Masquerade, but somehow never quite manage to make the grade. Personally, I don't see a need for that kind of power in Vampire. Everything you can imagine should be possible with a 5 dot devotion if it only uses a single discipline. If you need multiple disciplines then 5 dots of each would suffice. 6 dots would be plot devices, turn day into night, etc. Vampire isn't made to be comparable to Mage, or Werewolf. Themes are broken when you &quot;balance&quot; the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:01:44-07:00","id":612867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=612639#post612639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were some in first edition in some books but other approaches were done as well. And now 5 dot disciplines are much more powerful than what they were before.<br /> Some have even said the make 5 dot masquerade pale in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has more to do with Masquerade disciplines being are all over the place. Generally, 5 dots in Requiem is equal to 6-10 in Masquerade in terms of power. A devotion should be able to recreate anything in Masquerade that wasn't Antedeluvian, or very near.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:41:19-07:00","id":612888,"title":"","content":"So, making a devotion with one discipline plus blood potency 7-8-9-10, is definetely like have a discipline power over 6 right? And would be possible add a second discipline to make a devotion from 2 discipline power above 6 is it right???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:06:06-07:00","id":612932,"title":"","content":"Yup! Devotions are much more flexible this time around. For example, you can create a devotion requiring Vigor 5 and blood potency 6, and have it add an additional dot of strength for each dot of blood potency of 6 and higher (giving you the equivalent of Vigor 10 at BP 10), or you can have a devotion requiring Vigor 1, BP 6 and have it scale off your ranks in Vigor. If you want to be able to mesmerize crowds, then a devotion requiring dominate 1, BP 6 would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> There really isn't any limit to what you can do with devotions as long as it thematically fits with the prerequisites. The main problem is that we don't yet have any guidelines as to how to create mechanically balanced BP 6+ devotions. <br /> <br /> Now, the thing to remember is that each devotion should be treated as a single level of a given discipline. You can't have a devotion that uses Dominate 5, Vigor 5, bp 6 to give you the equivalent of both Dominate 6 and Vigor 6 for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7080-armadeo","name":"Armadeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:18:34-07:00","id":612942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=612888#post612888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, making a devotion with one discipline plus blood potency 7-8-9-10, is definetely like have a discipline power over 6 right? And would be possible add a second discipline to make a devotion from 2 discipline power above 6 is it right???</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the devotion Dark Decree. Prerequisites: Dominate 5, Majesty 4, Blood Potency 9.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.warosu.org/data/tg/img/0348/09/1410567382296.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T23:46:40-07:00","id":613054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=612888#post612888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, making a devotion with one discipline plus blood potency 7-8-9-10, is definetely like have a discipline power over 6 right? And would be possible add a second discipline to make a devotion from 2 discipline power above 6 is it right???</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a 5 dot devotion is equivalent to a discipline power that would be 5 or greater. There only being one discipline in Requiem that high it is hard to answer. It would be more precise to say anything you think a discipline should be able to do can be made into a devotion. If you would consider it a 10 dot discipline due to its power then it would be the same discipline but made as a devotion. You could consider adding Vigor to represent the added power the effect has. If the effect should require more than one discipline then you add that in.<br /> <br /> It might make more sense if you give an example of what you want to do or convert over from Masquerade. Whatever it is you would be thinking about when considering possibly using disciplines above 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T12:31:02-07:00","id":613827,"title":"","content":"Ngl, for physical disciplines I'd just have a Discipline 5, Blood Potency 6 Devotion for each that let you use your Blood Potency in place of your Discipline Dots for a scene at the cost of some vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T14:39:32-07:00","id":614049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'd like to point out that archmastery is not something every mage gets into. Very few mages past 5 Gnosis end up becoming archmages. While every vampire who turns a certain age while remaining active is going to be an elder.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on how you approach the concept. You could assume the &quot;elder&quot; here is a different state indeed. Look into Masquerade for the description of Methuselahs. Tough they are still vampires, the description is of monsters that suffer a strange change in psychology. Or you could look for D&amp;D's Demilich, an undead being that also represent not a lich simply too powerful, but truly achieving a kind of apotheosis. Again to Masquerade, in the Gehenna book you have a scenario where the Antes become very different beings by merging with the apotheotic state of their main powers.<br /> <br /> With that, you could easily rule that &quot;Elder Vampire&quot;, to this purpose, represent a transformative state, only possible with age and power, but not instantaneous with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To a vampire, an archmage is a plot device. Vampires don't need to have power at that level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Need for need, no one have. Mages didn't, either. But everyone can, and that would add to the game. Why doing it just for one?<br /> <br /> Elfive already said it very well, but let me add something.<br /> <br /> You are right in that high level vampires are equal to high level mages, not Archmages. That's precisely the point. As Archmages are a niche in itself, the Methuselah Vampires also are. It isn't about creating rules for high level play, this is covered by the core book itself. It is about creating rules for another tier of play entirely, with other themes and devices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some have even said the make 5 dot masquerade pale in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>All levels of Disciplines are more balanced on Requiem. I wouldn't say the 5 level powers allways make Masquerade pale in comparison, but some surely do. Certainly Oubliette is far more interesting as a standard 5th dot than Cloack the Gathering. But I felt way more difference in the 1st dots themselves. Now it REALLY pays out to have few dots in a variety of Disciplines, even 1 dot is enough to feel you XP was well spent. As a general rule they ended the notion of making a higher level power be just the low level on steroids, so each dot have its flavor and effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire isn't made to be comparable to Mage, or Werewolf. Themes are broken when you &quot;balance&quot; the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense you're thinking. But you failed to grasp what we're talking about. First, they ARE comparable. They live in the same setting, and follow the same basic rules. Of course they don't follow the same supernatural rules and they don't have to. As most people who argue against balance, you fail to understand the meaning of &quot;balance&quot;. In the simpler terms, we're not talking about making \u00fcber vampires that work the same way \u00fcber mages work. We're talking about making \u00fcber vampires in the sense a vampire would perceive an \u00fcber vampire. In the sense he is also a creature with the capacity to change world with his very existance. But with the themes, motifs and rules appropriate to such. Even if it end being just a suplement about how to make world-shaking Devotions. Probably not only that.<br /> <br /> Remember that a Mage is defined by Arcana, so it makes sense for an Archmage be defined by superior Arcana. A vampire is defined by his condition, by undeath and blood. Rules for Methuselah would probably work much more their very condition, the general rules of the Template, than tweak simple Disciplines. Those are the mechanical equivalents of Arcana, but not even close to being so defining of the vampire as Arcana are of the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T15:08:01-07:00","id":614167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=614049#post614049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends on how you approach the concept. You could assume the &quot;elder&quot; here is a different state indeed. Look into Masquerade for the description of Methuselahs. Tough they are still vampires, the description is of monsters that suffer a strange change in psychology. Or you could look for D&amp;D's Demilich, an undead being that also represent not a lich simply too powerful, but truly achieving a kind of apotheosis. Again to Masquerade, in the Gehenna book you have a scenario where the Antes become very different beings by merging with the apotheotic state of their main powers.<br /> <br /> With that, you could easily rule that &quot;Elder Vampire&quot;, to this purpose, represent a transformative state, only possible with age and power, but not instantaneous with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book for that is on the schedule.<br /> <br /> And you don't need more than 5 dots in a Discipline to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T19:26:07-07:00","id":614409,"title":"","content":"@monteparnas;<br /> <br /> Given that every time you state in an absolute sense what I'm thinking you are wrong, I would think that you would have caught on that you don't know what I'm thinking. Considering you talk about &quot;world-shaking&quot; powers, we seem to be in agreement as to what would be balanced. If you disagree then you are once again wrong as to what I'm thinking. I would suggest you check your ego, but I'm guessing that isn't possible for you, so until I get tired of humoring your misunderstandings (it is <i>your</i> fault when you go on about what is in my mind instead of what I say).<br /> <br /> Archmages <i>effectively</i> exist outside of the world of mage with their world shaking powers. Generally, Archmages are not supposed to meddle in the affairs of mages as they have ascended beyond them and have their rules against such things. Requiem, in the default case, has no place for uber vampires that secretly live alongside vampires sporting world shaking powers. It may not be a main theme of Requiem, but vampires are supposed to be powerful in their own continuum. Masquerade has these uber vampires (analogues to Archmasters) as you describe. They take the form of Antedeluvians and Inconnu. They don't fit in Requiem. Even neonates know elders and if one is in the city (they are rare) would know a Methuselah.<br /> <br /> You can't very well expect official material to break away from even lesser themes that exist within Requiem. Requiem is meant to be different than Masquerade. A group is welcome to play a game that is a hybrid of the two, but you are on your own at creating toys that fill that particular niche.<br /> <br /> Each game line exists in its own continuum. Vampire has creatures that are descriptively identical to werewolves and mages, but they are not, by default, Werewolves and Mages. Requiem is &quot;vampire world&quot; so vampires are not dwarfed by anything except more powerful vampires. Even the vampires that seek to evolve don't really want to evolve into a more powerful vampire. Vampires arrogantly believe they are the most powerful. The themes are different than Mage with its power-seeking protagonists. Mage needs Archmasters as they are a goal. Vampires would see an uber vampire as a regular vampire without","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T06:10:07-07:00","id":614928,"title":"","content":"My view on 6+ powers for Vampires is pretty cut and dried. I trust my players and fellow storytellers not to turn our chronicles into gonzo-fests enough, that I am extremely in favor of seeing advanced powers make it into official material. Even if I don't like them enough to use them, I know I'll buy the book and I know it will be a hit with others on both sides of the debate. Just like I bought Strange, Dead Love, even if it weren't my cup of tea.<br /> <br /> Also, an archmaster level will allow people like me, who enjoy millennia-spanning chronicles, to give a better ending to stories rather than the extremely anti-climatic &quot;We're in space now&quot; or &quot;You died&quot;, or the always unsatisfying &quot;Nothing left to throw at you folks&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T06:43:04-07:00","id":614963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=614928#post614928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view on 6+ powers for Vampires is pretty cut and dried. I trust my players and fellow storytellers not to turn our chronicles into gonzo-fests enough, that I am extremely in favor of seeing advanced powers make it into official material. Even if I don't like them enough to use them, I know I'll buy the book and I know it will be a hit with others on both sides of the debate. Just like I bought Strange, Dead Love, even if it weren't my cup of tea.<br /> <br /> Also, an archmaster level will allow people like me, who enjoy millennia-spanning chronicles, to give a better ending to stories rather than the extremely anti-climatic &quot;We're in space now&quot; or &quot;You died&quot;, or the always unsatisfying &quot;Nothing left to throw at you folks&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't think some of the devotions in the core aren't advanced?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The devotions in the core only scratch the surface as to what can be done too. IMO the covenant book has advanced powers and I would think the elder book will. Requiem is equal to Masquerade in power level without Requiem even having 6+ powers. Antedeluvian powers would require Requiem to break the 5 dot cap. Ants are not going to be official. It isn't just the plot that keeps them out of Requiem. Anyone that doubts the power of devotions should offer up an example power they think can only be represented by disciplines having more than 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T06:54:19-07:00","id":614992,"title":"","content":"One thing second edition has done is up the power of elders leaving long stretches of torpor. Attributes and skills over 5 don't drop when your blood potency does, for one thing. It seems the developers thought this would be harder to justify with disciplines and so effectively divorced them from blood potency completely. Blood potency is a measure of mystic muscle power. Disciplines are a measure of how well you can use it.<br /> <br /> It means a vastly ancient vampire that has fallen all the way to blood potency 1 still stands a chance against a 500 year old whelp with almost nothing but sheer might by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:31:22-07:00","id":615047,"title":"","content":"What is the effective difference between a six dot discipline and a devotion with high blood potency requirements? <br /> <br /> Where would one place a Majesty power that grants the vampire some sort of bonus for being worshiped like a god? Maybe worship grants the vampire willpower, or dice bonuses, Vitae, or a combination of the above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:52:32-07:00","id":615056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=615047#post615047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the effective difference between a six dot discipline and a devotion with high blood potency requirements? <br /> <br /> Where would one place a Majesty power that grants the vampire some sort of bonus for being worshiped like a god? Maybe worship grants the vampire willpower, or dice bonuses, Vitae, or a combination of the above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For most disciplines, there is none, but some disciplines levy situational penalties or grant bonus dice equal to your discipline rating. Devotions don't do that. And since additional ranks in disciplines don't increase in cost exponentially but obtaining out of clan powers is not only more expensive but come with unwanted side effects, it may be preferable for some to say their expertise with a certain discipline increases as well as branching out in a different direction after they reached the number 5 ceiling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T08:13:30-07:00","id":615096,"title":"","content":"Going deeper and broader with the same discipline could also be accomplished with single discipline devotions, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T08:16:24-07:00","id":615121,"title":"","content":"Oh, definitely. If you really need it to the bonus dice to the roll could theoretically be built in too. <br /> <br /> Maybe you could have a vigor devotion that doubles your effective dots with regard to feats of strength, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:15:06-07:00","id":615260,"title":"","content":"If the BP req is for using rather than learning then there isn't much of a difference, but why add things when you already have sufficient tools to do the job already? That can be confusing.<br /> <br /> If you just want to boost a discipline's power then a devotion that adds vigor seems to be the stock answer. I'm guessing Majesty 5 and Vigor to some degree. You could easily simulate 6+ that way by considering the Vigor as 6-10.<br /> <br /> If all Vigor 6 does is give you another point of strength, etc. then it would be kind of boring so a little devotion that acts as the experience drain would be just as good.<br /> <br /> Physical disciplines are arguably a case where it might be just as well to use higher disciplines, but as I'm not aware that stats can actually increase to more than 10 and that particular use of higher disciplines isn't really that impressive, I don't think that really fits uber-discipline like I expect from over 5 dots. I remember looking at Masquerade and thinking &quot;that's it?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:46:25-07:00","id":615291,"title":"","content":"After 5 dots you really need something a bit more impressive to make it worth the effort. Maybe a devotion that removes the limit that you can only select a given effect once per turn? <br /> <br /> That might be a bit too far on the other side, though. (punching for 75 damage, anyone?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T12:46:41-07:00","id":615475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=614409#post614409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@monteparnas;<br /> <br /> Given that every time you state in an absolute sense what I'm thinking you are wrong, I would think that you would have caught on that you don't know what I'm thinking. Considering you talk about &quot;world-shaking&quot; powers, we seem to be in agreement as to what would be balanced. If you disagree then you are once again wrong as to what I'm thinking. I would suggest you check your ego, but I'm guessing that isn't possible for you, so until I get tired of humoring your misunderstandings (it is <i>your</i> fault when you go on about what is in my mind instead of what I say).<br /> <br /> Archmages <i>effectively</i> exist outside of the world of mage with their world shaking powers. Generally, Archmages are not supposed to meddle in the affairs of mages as they have ascended beyond them and have their rules against such things. Requiem, in the default case, has no place for uber vampires that secretly live alongside vampires sporting world shaking powers. It may not be a main theme of Requiem, but vampires are supposed to be powerful in their own continuum. Masquerade has these uber vampires (analogues to Archmasters) as you describe. They take the form of Antedeluvians and Inconnu. They don't fit in Requiem. Even neonates know elders and if one is in the city (they are rare) would know a Methuselah.<br /> <br /> You can't very well expect official material to break away from even lesser themes that exist within Requiem. Requiem is meant to be different than Masquerade. A group is welcome to play a game that is a hybrid of the two, but you are on your own at creating toys that fill that particular niche.<br /> <br /> Each game line exists in its own continuum. Vampire has creatures that are descriptively identical to werewolves and mages, but they are not, by default, Werewolves and Mages. Requiem is &quot;vampire world&quot; so vampires are not dwarfed by anything except more powerful vampires. Even the vampires that seek to evolve don't really want to evolve into a more powerful vampire. Vampires arrogantly believe they are the most powerful. The themes are different than Mage with its power-seeking protagonists. Mage needs Archmasters as they are a goal. Vampires would see an uber vampire as a regular vampire without</div> </div> </div> </div>Beginning with a <u>mea culpa</u>, you are right. I was wrong on making assumptions about you thoughts or understanding, I misjudged and was simply too arrogant to my own good. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Except by the tales of Atlantis, about the Exarchs and Oracles, Mage wasn't supposed to go to such tier, either. It was a possibility, but never a given part of the game. The same goes for any other splat. In every one, is implied that the power of a very high level member is godlike, and we are just talking about high Power Trait. Even Mage don't need an Archmaster status to do that. A Mage with high Gnosis and a lot of high-level Arcana are a frightening power on his own. The things you can do with such combination already amounts to rewrite reality on a fearsome scale.<br /> <br /> What Archmasters do is to bring the game to a new tier of play. Where a city ceases to be your main concern and becomes just your home. Country to Global spanning stories cease to be your great feats to become your daily affairs. And your great feats amount to cosmic scale. And that's it. Mage is as meant to do that as Vampire or Werewolf. It is a game about street-level modern magic. The struggles between the Orders and the search for the Mysteries can bring the game to Global conspiracy and a lot of globetrotting, but those aren't missing in Vampire, Werewolf or Changeling at all. Covenants also span the entire world and struggle in greater schemes, and all of them also have interests and mysteries that can easily bring a coterie to as much traveling as any cabal, even if at more danger. Werewolves and Changelings both deal with creatures with far reaching influence and power, and it can be even easier for them to extend their affairs across countries, continents, and even worlds, for if Mage have an easier time with strange spheres of existence, those creatures naturally live between worlds.<br /> <br /> In no sense Mage goes beyond them in scope by itself. Archmasters aren't less of a departure from common Mage than Methuselahs would be, or Ancestral Spirit Werewolfs, or Once Changeling True Faes. And none are a departure from all the tropes of the games as you say. Sure, a departure from the initial proposition on play-style. This initial proposition isn't supposed to work on such a tier. Hence the greater tier being presented in another book. Its a new take, optional, that can either played or presented as background, or be completely absent, depending on the tastes of the troupe and the necessities of he chronicle. That's an option, and the other games are as valid for such option as Mage. Masquerade had vampires analogue to Archmasters, but it was presented just as an example. I could as well use Castlevania, a game where vampires are the most powerful beings around. I presented an example of the trope from D&amp;D. I'm not saying Requiem should be made into Masquerade, D&amp;D or Castlevania, they where just examples of an existing trope. And I AM saying that Archmasters don't fit in Mage either by your reasoning.<br /> <br /> And no, each game line ISN'T its own continuum. THAT is an assumption from cWoD, not nWoD. You can look again in the books, there are NO creatures described to be identical to the ones in other lines. The game <u><b>explicitly</b></u> says that vampires, werewolves, mages and changelings, among others, are described in their own books. It assumes you don't need to do crossovers but if you do they are crossovers, with complete support from the rules. Vampires ARE powerseeking and HAVE legends about \u00fcber vampires. The creation myth of the Lancea et Sanctum is about it, as are both the myth and raison d'etre of the Ordo Dracul, the fears of the Carthians and both fears and hopes of the Invictus, and the underlying assumptions around both the source of vampirism and the Strixes. The nWoD was made as a toolbox setting, where all parts are interchangeable. There are no such a thing as a closed setting, just a possibility of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the effective difference between a six dot discipline and a devotion with high blood potency requirements?</div> </div> </div> </div>None.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going deeper and broader with the same discipline could also be accomplished with single discipline devotions, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For most disciplines, there is none, but some disciplines levy situational penalties or grant bonus dice equal to your discipline rating. Devotions don't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Devotions can make the bonuses and penalties use other traits or combinations of Disciplines, so the point is moot. They can still augment anything beyond 5th dot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical disciplines are arguably a case where it might be just as well to use higher disciplines, but as I'm not aware that stats can actually increase to more than 10 and that particular use of higher disciplines isn't really that impressive, I don't think that really fits uber-discipline like I expect from over 5 dots. I remember looking at Masquerade and thinking &quot;that's it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one Devotion with Discipline 5 + BP 6+ should do the trick. It could cost more than a single dot of he Discipline or work for just one aspect of it, demand two or three Devotions to work the entire Discipline, but that's it. After this threshold I wouldn't bother to demand XP for every &quot;dot above 5&quot; for simple augment. One house rule of mine on Masquerade was that you would receive the common effect of those Disciplines along with the true high-level effects if you bought them. Not very balanced, I know, but otherwise it seemed simply boring (the main effects where too useful in Masquerade to not take).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">After 5 dots you really need something a bit more impressive to make it worth the effort. Maybe a devotion that removes the limit that you can only select a given effect once per turn? <br /> <br /> That might be a bit too far on the other side, though. (punching for 75 damage, anyone?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:03:12-07:00","id":615494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=615475#post615475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, each game line ISN'T its own continuum. THAT is an assumption from cWoD, not nWoD. You can look again in the books, there are NO creatures described to be identical to the ones in other lines. The game <u><b>explicitly</b></u> says that vampires, werewolves, mages and changelings, among others, are described in their own books. It assumes you don't need to do crossovers but if you do they are crossovers, with complete support from the rules. Vampires ARE powerseeking and HAVE legends about \u00fcber vampires. The creation myth of the Lancea et Sanctum is about it, as are both the myth and raison d'etre of the Ordo Dracul, the fears of the Carthians and both fears and hopes of the Invictus, and the underlying assumptions around both the source of vampirism and the Strixes. The nWoD was made as a toolbox setting, where all parts are interchangeable. There are no such a thing as a closed setting, just a possibility of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each nWoD game (with the possible exception of Beast) is designed to stand alone, but be compatible with the other lines. This can be a bit confusing, as the books certainly do address other supernatural beings. But there is no attempt to make unified world, and developers do not worry themselves with cross-splat balance when designing their games. So it's not quite correct to say that nWoD all takes place in its on continuum, nor that they take place together, but rather that nWoD has a highly flexible continuum that assumes storyteller meddling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T16:16:37-07:00","id":615690,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure they worry with cross-splat balance, and can easily see that it does happen. That is a necessity to address the possibility of crossover.<br /> <br /> That said, yeah, nWoD don't have its own unified continuum, NOR a distinct continuum for each line. It have a toolbox for the ST to determine the chronicle's own continuum.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite from cWoD, that had BOTH closed-box continuum for each line and a unified crossed continuum, with a pretty confuse result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T18:28:19-07:00","id":615877,"title":"","content":"It is complicated so I might not be explaining it well. It has been the case from the beginning of Requiem that the werewolves in Requiem might or might not be the werewolves in Forsaken. You can stat werewolves using Requiem mechanics and some hand-waiving, which is the default situation unless you play a Requiem/Forsaken game. They are completely compatible so you can indeed play a combined game of Requiem and Forsaken, but that is not the default. They actually don't worry much about cross-over. They don't try to make vampires and werewolves balanced in any way. If you want to have both in your game by using both lines then you can balance them how you want. They leave it to a group that wants to do it. Vampires are balanced. Werewolves are balanced. Everything is balanced within its own line, but not balanced to other lines. It's hard to explain. Forsaken doesn't exist if you play Requiem unless you want it to exist. They write as if it does, not as if it must. They went for an interesting approach. It is a bit different than Classic.<br /> <br /> PS: @monteparnas no problem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:27:00-07:00","id":616051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=615690#post615690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure they worry with cross-splat balance, and can easily see that it does happen. That is a necessity to address the possibility of crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>They look for internal consistency, and a certain thematic (personal horror), but basically every developer has said at one point or another that they don't give a piss about crossover balance. Conveniently, at least thus far in 2e, the developers have all focused on making the splats awesome to play. So even if they aren't all &quot;balanced&quot; (a largely subjective concept) in crossover, they are all fun, and that's really what counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-05-2015, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:50:14-07:00","id":616069,"title":"","content":"What PenDragon said. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T13:42:02-07:00","id":616786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=615877#post615877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is complicated so I might not be explaining it well. It has been the case from the beginning of Requiem that the werewolves in Requiem might or might not be the werewolves in Forsaken. You can stat werewolves using Requiem mechanics and some hand-waiving, which is the default situation unless you play a Requiem/Forsaken game. They are completely compatible so you can indeed play a combined game of Requiem and Forsaken, but that is not the default. They actually don't worry much about cross-over. They don't try to make vampires and werewolves balanced in any way. If you want to have both in your game by using both lines then you can balance them how you want. They leave it to a group that wants to do it. Vampires are balanced. Werewolves are balanced. Everything is balanced within its own line, but not balanced to other lines. It's hard to explain. Forsaken doesn't exist if you play Requiem unless you want it to exist. They write as if it does, not as if it must. They went for an interesting approach. It is a bit different than Classic.<br /> <br /> PS: @monteparnas no problem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>How do you build weres for requiem?<br /> Not that I don't like forsaken.. I just feel their Weres detract from the themes in vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T18:00:17-07:00","id":616986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=616786#post616786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you build weres for requiem?<br /> Not that I don't like forsaken.. I just feel their Weres detract from the themes in vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>You use Disciplines and Devotions for their powers and handwave anything that doesn't cover. You would probably give them Resilience instead of Regeneration for instance. You would give them different Protean dots for the shapeshifting. Basically, you make a werewolf whatever you want and at whatever power level you want, but you use Vampire powers to get it done. I wouldn't do it unless I want to remove the spirit stuff from and simplify werewolves which actually makes sense in a Requiem game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-05-2015, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T20:22:21-07:00","id":617104,"title":"","content":"You could build a &quot;Lupine&quot; as something like the Ghuls from Wicked Dead, immortal daywalking creatures with Protean and some kind of special power that turns them into a giant wolf man at some times, but they gain Vitae from eating flesh like Ghuls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T02:58:07-07:00","id":617412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=616786#post616786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just feel their Weres detract from the themes in vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a setting. If the mere existence of the forsaken can ruin the themes of vampire they didn't really exist in the first place. They were simply an illusion the protagonists surrounded themselves with, ready to be shattered with the sledgehammer called &quot;reality&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T03:13:13-07:00","id":617426,"title":"","content":"I don't understand why werewolf or mage or other supernatural creatures should ruins the vampire setting. I think it give more complexity and variability to the game. Then you could chose to don't use directly in your story and let these creature just as myths or legends amongs the undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T03:17:04-07:00","id":617453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5#post608558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do exist any official example of disciplines powers above fifth for the second edition of requiem? Or any unofficial but plausible homemade powers on web??</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Devotions can accomplish the same effects as Tier 6+ disciplines, I think. There's one that combines Protean with Celerity that speeds up your shape shifting to instant speed. Imagine a vampire who can turn into mist in the blink of an eye to bypass an attack, then solidify again and go on the offensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T05:37:25-07:00","id":617635,"title":"","content":"I can see how werewolves and mages might get in the way of a Requiem game. Shadow, Astral, all that weird stuff. You can strip that away, but for antagonists it might be easier to just use the tools in Requiem to build what you want. For player characters, you seem better off starting with something from another book than building a template from scratch. I think Skinchangers has werewolves of a sort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T06:06:41-07:00","id":617674,"title":"","content":"You could also just use a wolfblood with a shifting tell. Keeps things relatively simple <i>and</i> you get to play with &quot;actually, that wasn't a <i>real</i> werewolf&quot; rumours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T08:08:29-07:00","id":617777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=617426#post617426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why werewolf or mage or other supernatural creatures should ruins the vampire setting. I think it give more complexity and variability to the game. Then you could chose to don't use directly in your story and let these creature just as myths or legends amongs the undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me explain. I love Mage the Acension. And would probably like Awakening if I got chance to play.<br /> However Mages in both those games are WAY too powerful for vamps. If I want mages in my Vamp game they will be what used to call hedge wizards.<br /> Same with Weres. While I like what I've of forsaken, I don't think their lore adds to a Vamp world and again they are way too powerful from a traditional folklore point of view.<br /> I while weres should scary even to vamps they should not steamroll them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T15:35:18-07:00","id":618154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=617777#post617777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me explain. I love Mage the Acension. And would probably like Awakening if I got chance to play.<br /> However Mages in both those games are WAY too powerful for vamps. If I want mages in my Vamp game they will be what used to call hedge wizards.<br /> Same with Weres. While I like what I've of forsaken, I don't think their lore adds to a Vamp world and again they are way too powerful from a traditional folklore point of view.<br /> I while weres should scary even to vamps they should not steamroll them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well being way too powerful might explain why the clans have a big, red &quot;Keep the fuck away&quot; sign listed on their stereotypes next to Werewolves and Mages.<br /> <br /> When I was first getting introduced to World of Darkness, the levels of power were explained to me once and they went something a little bit like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1 Werewolf = 5 vampires in a fight.<br /> <br /> 1 Mage = city destroying power level.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires don't go trompsing around werewolf territory because A) they are too powerful by themselves, and B) They don't travel by themselves! Werewolves are going to be even more powerful in 2e, as I've read they can apparently heal all their wounds <b>in 1 turn</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires also treat mages with caution because that fight would equate to Superman vs Mxyzptlk in terms of ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> The different splats for WoD are not inherently meant to be crossed over. There may be lupines in a vampire game, but that doesn't mean they're the same lupines from Forsaken. Same way around with vampires in a werewolf run game, or both creatures in a mage game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beast: the Primordial is the first game that's specifically designed to include cross over stories and has been met with mixed opinions on that subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-06-2015, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T15:56:52-07:00","id":618163,"title":"","content":"That must be referring to old World of Darkness. First edition werewolves in new World could be taken out by a vampire right out of character creation.<br /> <br /> Anyways, vampires and werewolves are a fun thing to play with and while every mention of it on the forum seems to suggest they are constantly at war and trying to mindlessly kill each other on sight in their white rooms, there's no reason to actually play it that way. So you have werewolves as a sort of outside of the box neutral party. They can be antagonists or allies, they both share the night and have a form of Masquerade. They represent enough of the population and travel in enough of similar circles that they are an issue that should be appreciated one way or another. A story arc in my last vampire game involved the death of the previous liaison to werewolves and the members of court, including a player, who were trying to take up the position, involving a strong diplomatic connection to werewolves through their more renowned packs.<br /> <br /> I've been reading about the werewolves from vampire being different werewolves but I'm not sure how accurate that is, I'd seriously need to see a page suggesting that was the case if I was going to. I believe that was an old World of Darkness thing as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T16:33:27-07:00","id":618206,"title":"","content":"Y'know, the requiem 2e book never actually <i>uses</i> the word &quot;lupine&quot;. And the few references to werewolves there are also mention Gifts and Primal Urge, so I'm forced to come to the conclusion that, no, in second edition the werewolves mentioned in the vampire books are indeed the Uratha in their full spirity glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T16:46:48-07:00","id":618213,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the power level of other splats. If anything, I agree that each splat should come in its own mini-container. Other than that, we've had these 6+ threads before, and I always want to ask posters that disagree the same question: &quot;Look me with a straight eye and tell me, would you really not buy a book about Methuselahs with arch-level powers?&quot;. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T16:46:53-07:00","id":618214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is complicated so I might not be explaining it well. It has been the case from the beginning of Requiem that the werewolves in Requiem might or might not be the werewolves in Forsaken. You can stat werewolves using Requiem mechanics and some hand-waiving, which is the default situation unless you play a Requiem/Forsaken game. They are completely compatible so you can indeed play a combined game of Requiem and Forsaken, but that is not the default. They actually don't worry much about cross-over. They don't try to make vampires and werewolves balanced in any way. If you want to have both in your game by using both lines then you can balance them how you want. They leave it to a group that wants to do it. Vampires are balanced. Werewolves are balanced. Everything is balanced within its own line, but not balanced to other lines. It's hard to explain. Forsaken doesn't exist if you play Requiem unless you want it to exist. They write as if it does, not as if it must. They went for an interesting approach. It is a bit different than Classic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tough it is easy for someone used to cWoD to use rules of one splat to represent other creatures, it isn't how the game is intended to work on nWoD. Lets just see Requiem 1st ed:<br /> <br /> Pages 114 and 115, about Supernatural Conflict. Through the entire text Disciplines are referred to exclusively as vampiric powers. The text talks about how other supernatural creatures resist to them, but it is fairly explicit in saying they may have or not equivalents to Blood Potency, but not BP itself. It talks about how a vampire resist to their powers with BP, but makes it clear such powers aren't Disciplines. And in the end <b>explicitly</b> says the rules about such creatures are &quot;addressed in Werewolf: The Forsaken, Mage: The Awakening and other Storytelling games&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just searched for it through the entire book, and saw no reference to use of werewolves or other creatures by Requiem's rules. The book does assume such creatures exist, but it makes no other assumption about them. Instead, it focus on vampires, sure, and simply say to the ST to <u>look for other lines for information on other creatures</u>, no support to work them without the proper line whatsoever. Of course you can do this and of course you can also bring the rules of other lines and drop their own fluff entirely, but that ISN'T an assumption of the game or how it is intended to run. By the way, there are even canon cross-over setting, the city of Chicago IIRC, as far as canon go in nWoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see how werewolves and mages might get in the way of a Requiem game. Shadow, Astral, all that weird stuff. You can strip that away, but for antagonists it might be easier to just use the tools in Requiem to build what you want. For player characters, you seem better off starting with something from another book than building a template from scratch. I think Skinchangers has werewolves of a sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personaly I think the places of power and other worlds of those games make for solid Dragon Nests for the Ordo Dracul. In fact, exploring the other lines and possible truths and myths among other supernaturals makes for a very interesting chronicle. The Ordo would want the knowledge, while the other four Covenants where look for ways to turn those things to their own side, or just act to suppress knowledge of them from vampiric society.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying there are anything wrong with ruling out some or all other splats from a given chronicle. I think it work much more in a chronicle-by-chronicle basis than as a general rule. That's why the setting is toolbox-like to begin with. But that said, more tools are more tools, more options of building blocks for your chronicle. Surely there are chronicles where I can pretty much see other splats stealing the spotlight from the one you intend to run, and so it is better to rule them out as they are. In others, the same presence of splats can <b>sharpen</b> the spotlight by contrast.<br /> <br /> By the way, werewolves are combat machines on 2nd ed, but far from so much more powerful. With the right build a vampire can overcome most werewolves in single combat, and group combat have so much variables that they hardly can be said on advantage in a fight between a pack and a coterie of the same size. The regeneration thing is only in a very limited in use Killing Form that easily leads them to frenzy. And their frenzy is far worse than a vampire one in power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading about the werewolves from vampire being different werewolves but I'm not sure how accurate that is, I'd seriously need to see a page suggesting that was the case if I was going to. I believe that was an old World of Darkness thing as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't accurate at all. You can surely run things like that if you want, but I can guarantee you, no nWoD book support such idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T18:55:24-07:00","id":618305,"title":"","content":"Unless the book had something else in it that I thought might actually be useful then I would definitely not buy such a book. *looking straight at the screen*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T19:03:20-07:00","id":618309,"title":"","content":"I'd buy two, and send one to Diggs, just because. =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T19:39:34-07:00","id":618340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=618309#post618309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd buy two, and send one to Diggs, just because. =P</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T20:30:01-07:00","id":618395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=618213#post618213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the power level of other splats. If anything, I agree that each splat should come in its own mini-container. Other than that, we've had these 6+ threads before, and I always want to ask posters that disagree the same question: &quot;Look me with a straight eye and tell me, would you really not buy a book about Methuselahs with arch-level powers?&quot;. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>On the subject 5+ disciplines, I used to be in your camp . But I no longer think it is necessary. I really don't.<br /> <br /> As to wolfs and Mages .<br /> MtA either version are games about hubris and power. They were not meant to be balanced against vamps In their world vamps are mooks.<br /> Same with weres. BTW where in traditional mythos do you get werewolves are shamans? every single one of them?<br /> Like I said I'd love to play Forsaken(sipdar are you listening?).<br /> But I think those kind of weres would detract from the vamp story as would Awakening mages.<br /> <br /> Yes I want hermetic rivals to my vamps. But I want a ritualistic feel and something not as powerful as Awakening(which I want to play as well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T21:13:54-07:00","id":618430,"title":"","content":"You have Sons of Phobos in Blood Sorcery to cover mages or you could use Theban as it is with some flavor changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:00:37-07:00","id":618463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=618430#post618430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have Sons of Phobos in Blood Sorcery to cover mages or you could use Theban as it is with some flavor changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but not just theban. Cruac where a mortal must get blood somewhere makes a very dark magic. But the developers hate that notion. They want to stay vamp specific.<br /> Witch hunters and second sight both offer interesting rules as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:16:22-07:00","id":618502,"title":"","content":"As was already pointed, the books DO assume that, if you are using the equivalent of a major splat, you are using the splat itself, not a weaker version.<br /> <br /> Either way, WoD: Mirrors already have rules for magic using splat-powers as basis. You can make each Ritual into a Merit 1 dot higher than the level of the ritual, to use with Second Sight's rules for mortal ritual magic. I would adjust it further to be only dot = level in case of rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:22:56-07:00","id":618506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=618395#post618395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same with weres. BTW where in traditional mythos do you get werewolves are shamans? every single one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh~ kind of hard to place that, really. Yeah it's true that Werewolves walk around with the spirits practically 24/7, but the level of proficiency they have can vary from one member to another. Only the actual shaman-shamans make a career out of dealing with the spirit world. The other auspices usually do it when it's necessary and lack the same level of skill or knowledge when doing so.<br /> <br /> Imagine a tribal society who believes in the spirit world. Every member of the tribe knows spirits exist and they may try to invoke them at times, but usually they have a specially appointed individual (Medicine Men, Wisemen, Shaman, Priests, est) who handle any of the big rituals and ceremonies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T22:25:26-07:00","id":618508,"title":"","content":"I confess my knowledge about awakening is just partial, I have to read better the book. But watching at the magic I didn't see too much superiority against a vampire. In a face to face fight at least. Probably you are right cause you know the game better than me. This is just an impression...just the magic whit which they can create a little sun is definitely deadly against a vampire in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-07-2015, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T23:17:13-07:00","id":618568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=618463#post618463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True but not just theban. Cruac where a mortal must get blood somewhere makes a very dark magic. But the developers hate that notion. They want to stay vamp specific.<br /> Witch hunters and second sight both offer interesting rules as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cruac is what the Sons of Phobos use for magic, vitae and all IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T04:21:39-07:00","id":618676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=618568#post618568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cruac is what the Sons of Phobos use for magic, vitae and all IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But the sons of phobos are something else entirely as well apparently immortal.<br /> The somehow consume the heart of humans and get &quot;vitae&quot; from that. While turning the human into some sort of drone akin to original haitian zombie . Alive but under the will of the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T05:24:05-07:00","id":618694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=618676#post618676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But the sons of phobos are something else entirely as well apparently immortal.<br /> The somehow consume the heart of humans and get &quot;vitae&quot; from that. While turning the human into some sort of drone akin to original haitian zombie . Alive but under the will of the mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so necromancers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You wanted a different type of mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T08:37:43-07:00","id":618963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/608558-disciplines-level-above-5?p=618395#post618395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to wolfs and Mages .<br /> MtA either version are games about hubris and power. They were not meant to be balanced against vamps In their world vamps are mooks.<br /> Same with weres. BTW where in traditional mythos do you get werewolves are shamans? every single one of them?<br /> Like I said I'd love to play Forsaken(sipdar are you listening?).<br /> But I think those kind of weres would detract from the vamp story as would Awakening mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not had that experience in our campaigns. Werewolves, Mages and Vampires play very well together, right out of the core books, at least in my experience. <br /> <br /> Shifting alliances and power struggles abounded in our campaign, involving all the big 3, plus Changelings. And it was pretty awesome. Some Were's were more powerful than Changelings, Vampires or Mages, and vice versa (and there was a healthy amount of respect amongst all the supernaturals when it came to confrontations, as one could never be entirely positive about the power players of the city). They all had their Niche's and their strengths and weaknesses, and they played off of each other really, really well. The themes of each splat were prevalent and pervasive and never clashed with the themes of the others (even when their agendas clashed). Of course, POV of characters may have been at odds with certain themes of other splats (The Blood Rites of certain Vampires really squicked out a werewolf or two, while the practices of the Cahalith Hunter in Darkness made everyone nervous, even the powerful changelings, mages and vampires), but that is character development, not true theme clash. In the end, it made for an amazing and awesome setting. Can't wait to get back to it, hopefully really soon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}